WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.753 --> 00:00:06.340
(fly buzzing)

00:00:06.423 --> 00:00:09.593
♪ The yellow sunshine... ♪

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:11.720
- Yimana, who Sylviane
was based on,

00:00:11.803 --> 00:00:15.182
came to America to go to
a 2-year silent retreat.

00:00:16.391 --> 00:00:17.851
It started to feel like
this metaphor

00:00:17.935 --> 00:00:20.103
for the whole experience
of coming to America,

00:00:20.187 --> 00:00:22.564
like the weirdness
of a silent retreat,

00:00:22.648 --> 00:00:25.108
and that you're looking
to pick up on human behaviors.

00:00:25.192 --> 00:00:27.194
Now look around
at people's props.

00:00:27.277 --> 00:00:30.030
You should've maybe
got more pillows.

00:00:30.113 --> 00:00:32.866
People have some other stuff
that looks cozier.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.662
In a way, the silence in the episode
was almost like the great equalizer

00:00:36.745 --> 00:00:39.414
because once
you took away language,

00:00:39.498 --> 00:00:42.334
no one knew she was...
a foreigner.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:46.922
Because the episode
was in silence,

00:00:47.005 --> 00:00:49.800
you needed visual ways to explore
what was happening in her brain.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:53.595
I decided that Sylviane was
going to have these weird hallucinations.

00:00:56.014 --> 00:00:59.726
♪ Take my hand,
follow me ♪

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:03.981
♪ To the bay behind the sea ♪

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:07.401
- This episode explores the ways
we're all different,

00:01:07.484 --> 00:01:10.028
and how that can prevent
connection sometimes.

00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:12.030
But I think the cool thing
about this episode

00:01:12.114 --> 00:01:14.700
is it shows much more
about how we're all alike

00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:16.618
than how we're all different.

